 "equipment_type": "Pressure-independent 6-way control valve",
 "applies_to": "SAUTER eValveco UVC106BF electronic pressure-independent 6-port (change-over) valves for 4-pipe climate ceilings and similar, DN15 and DN25.",
 "summary": "The UVC106BF is a motorised 6-port ball valve with its own flow measurement and controller, used to switch a single coil between heating and cooling circuits. The BF variants have a BACnet MS/TP interface; the handbook lists binary, analog input, analog value, analog output and multistate value objects: flow and temperatures, heating/cooling setpoints (Y1h/Y1c or flow Vsh/Vsc), room temperature control settings, energy, climate status and configuration.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Firmware 0.8.3 or higher, application 4.06.09 or higher",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names are short codes as printed; the descriptions here are from the handbook's variables annex and section 2.",
  "Many objects are marked as present only on some product types (handbook footnotes); not every object exists in every valve.",
  "AV 25 and AV 26 are both printed as \"Window Open\" (ranges 6-35 °C and 6-40 °C); the annex calls the pair Window Open MinTemp and MaxTemp without saying which instance is which.",
  "Several AVs (Y1h, Y1c, Vsh, Troom, Tsetadj) also have writable Low/High Limit properties that set their range; those are properties, not separate objects.",
  "Units are not printed per object; temperatures follow Temp Unit (BV 16), energy is Wh or BTU, flow in the unit set on the device.",
  "Source: handbook chapter 6.4-6.7, Tab. 13, 15, 18, 20 and 22, pages 40-48 (62 objects). The Modbus lists in chapter 5 also cover UVC102/UVC103."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "eValveco UVC10x Handbook",
  "doc_number": "P100017780 Version 02 Revision 01",
